293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 245 0 R
/E (Traditional QR codes provide unrestricted access once scanned, exposing users to fraud risks such as phishing, malware distribution, credential theft, and unauthorized data access. Existing QR solutions prioritize convenience over security and lack encryption, access control, and monitoring, making QR codes an increasingly exploited attack vector in modern digital environments.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
