520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1105 0 R
/E (TLS 1.3 \(Transport Layer Security\) is the latest cryptographic protocol that encrypts data between client and server to prevent eavesdropping and tampering. It provides faster handshakes, reduced latency with 0-RTT \(early data\), and stronger security by supporting only modern ciphers with Perfect Forward Secrecy.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1106 0 R
/E (ChaCha20-Poly1305 is an AEAD \(Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data\) cipher used in TLS 1.3. ChaCha20 provides fast, stream-based encryption resistant to timing attacks, while Poly1305 ensures integrity and authenticity, detecting any tampering. Together, TLS 1.3 with ChaCha20-Poly1305 ensures HTTPS data is confidential, authenticated, and tamper-proof, even on devices without AES hardware acceleration.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
